# {{ benchmark_name }} Service

## Getting started

Edit `src/{{ benchmark_package }}/benchmark_service.py` and implement the six abstract methods on `ExampleBenchmark`:

| Method | What to do |
|--------|------------|
| `load_datasets()` | Return `dict[dataset_name, dict[task_id, ...]]` of all datasets |
| `retrieve_task()` | Return sandbox source, problem statement, and resource requirements |
| `setup_task()` | Prepare the sandbox before evaluation (upload files, run install commands) |
| `evaluate_response()` | Score a plain-text response without a sandbox |
| `evaluate_instance()` | Run tests / evaluation scripts in the sandbox |
| `calculate_final_score()` | Aggregate per-task results into a single score |

`setup_task` and `evaluate_instance` are async generators — yield `StreamMessageChunk`, `StreamErrorChunk`, and finally `StreamResultChunk`.

## Authentication

{% if template == "vals-ai" %}
The Vals layer lives in `src/{{ benchmark_package }}/vals_ai/`. `ExampleBenchmark` subclasses `ValsBenchmarkService`; `main.py` uses `ValsBenchmarkServiceApp`. Both inherit the shared classes. The Vals app adds the `/v1/*` routes.

Set `AUTH_REQUIRED=true` to enable Descope authentication, catalog/allowlist access, quotas, and trial restrictions. Configure `DESCOPE_PROJECT_ID` and access through `BENCHMARK_CATALOG_API_URL` plus `SERVICE_NAME`, `DESCOPE_TENANT_ALLOWLIST_JSON`, or `DESCOPE_ALLOWLIST_PATH`. Requests then require a Descope access key in `X-Descope-Api-Key`. Quota-enabled services also require `SERVICE_NAME` and `EVALUATION_QUOTA_TABLE_NAME`.

Framework upgrades do not update these copied files. Local `/v1/*` requests work without credentials when `AUTH_REQUIRED` is unset or false.
{% else %}
Set `AUTH_REQUIRED=true` to require authentication. Implement `check_auth()` for boolean authentication, or `resolve_tenant()` and `check_dataset_access()` for tenant-aware access. With authentication required, the default rejects requests until you implement these hooks. This app includes the shared HTTP and WebSocket routes; it has no `/v1/*` routes.
{% endif %}

Authentication is disabled by default. Hosted registry deployments set `AUTH_REQUIRED=true`. `AUTH_DISABLED` is no longer supported and cannot override that setting.

